  "html": "<p class=\"kicker\">Course coverage</p>\n<h1>OWASP coverage</h1>\n<p class=\"prose\">Three OWASP lists, entry by entry, with the lessons that cite each entry. Use it to find the lesson for a finding, and to see what the course leaves out.</p>\n<p class=\"prose meta\">Generated from the 33 lesson pages by <code>tools/build_coverage.py</code>. Do not edit this file by hand. A lesson is listed when its page names the entry's id. That is a low bar: a lesson that names an entry once is listed beside one that is built around it. These lists set no requirements, and covering every entry does not make an API secure.</p>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"api\">\n<h2 id=\"api\">OWASP API Security Top 10 2023</h2>\n<p class=\"meta\"><a href=\"https://api-security.owasp.org/editions/2023/en/0x11-t10/\">OWASP API Security Top 10 2023</a>. 2023 edition, the newest.</p>\n<div class=\"wrap\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Entry</th><th>Lessons that cite it</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>API1:2023 Broken Object Level Authorization</td><td><a href=\"../topics/object-level-authorization/index.html\">Module 9, Object-level authorization</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>API2:2023 Broken Authentication</td><td><a href=\"../topics/authentication-endpoints/index.html\">Module 27, Attacks on authentication endpoints</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>API3:2023 Broken Object Property Level Authorization</td><td><a href=\"../topics/property-and-function-authorization/index.html\">Module 10, Property and function authorization</a>; <a href=\"../topics/data-in-model-context/index.html\">Module 24, Data in model context</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>API4:2023 Unrestricted Resource Consumption</td><td><a href=\"../topics/request-and-response-contracts/index.html\">Module 13, Request and response contracts</a>; <a href=\"../topics/rate-limiting-and-cost/index.html\">Module 15, Rate limiting and cost controls</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>API5:2023 Broken Function Level Authorization</td><td><a href=\"../topics/property-and-function-authorization/index.html\">Module 10, Property and function authorization</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>API6:2023 Unrestricted Access to Sensitive Business Flows</td><td><a href=\"../topics/business-flows-and-idempotency/index.html\">Module 11, Business flows and idempotency</a>; <a href=\"../topics/logging-and-detection/index.html\">Module 30, Logging, detection and response</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>API7:2023 Server Side Request Forgery</td><td><a href=\"../topics/ssrf-and-unsafe-consumption/index.html\">Module 14, SSRF and unsafe consumption of APIs</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>API8:2023 Security Misconfiguration</td><td><a href=\"../topics/security-misconfiguration/index.html\">Module 29, Security misconfiguration</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>API9:2023 Improper Inventory Management</td><td><a href=\"../topics/gateway-enforcement/index.html\">Module 12, Gateway enforcement</a>; <a href=\"../topics/versioning-and-deprecation/index.html\">Module 18, Versioning and deprecation</a>; <a href=\"../topics/security-misconfiguration/index.html\">Module 29, Security misconfiguration</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>API10:2023 Unsafe Consumption of APIs</td><td><a href=\"../topics/ssrf-and-unsafe-consumption/index.html\">Module 14, SSRF and unsafe consumption of APIs</a></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"llm\">\n<h2 id=\"llm\">OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026</h2>\n<p class=\"meta\"><a href=\"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/\">OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026</a>. Version 2026, August 2026. The title page of the document reads &quot;OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications 2026&quot;.</p>\n<div class=\"wrap\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Entry</th><th>Lessons that cite it</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>LLM01:2026 Prompt Injection</td><td><a href=\"../topics/prompt-injection-and-output-handling/index.html\">Module 22, Prompt injection and output handling</a>; <a href=\"../topics/agent-authority-and-approvals/index.html\">Module 23, Agent authority and approvals</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>LLM02:2026 Sensitive Information Disclosure</td><td><a href=\"../topics/data-in-model-context/index.html\">Module 24, Data in model context</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>LLM03:2026 Excessive Agency</td><td><a href=\"../topics/agent-authority-and-approvals/index.html\">Module 23, Agent authority and approvals</a>; <a href=\"../topics/agent-containment/index.html\">Module 31, Agent code execution and containment</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>LLM04:2026 Supply Chain</td><td><a href=\"../topics/supply-chain-retrieval-and-memory/index.html\">Module 25, Supply chain, retrieval, and memory</a>; <a href=\"../topics/model-supply-chain/index.html\">Module 32, Model and artifact supply chain</a><br><span class=\"meta\">Module 32 teaches the entry: models, adapters, converted files and packages taken in from outside. Module 25 teaches the data side only. On-device models are named in module 32 and not taught.</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>LLM05:2026 Data and Model Poisoning</td><td><a href=\"../topics/supply-chain-retrieval-and-memory/index.html\">Module 25, Supply chain, retrieval, and memory</a>; <a href=\"../topics/model-supply-chain/index.html\">Module 32, Model and artifact supply chain</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>LLM06:2026 Unbounded Consumption</td><td><a href=\"../topics/rate-limiting-and-cost/index.html\">Module 15, Rate limiting and cost controls</a>; <a href=\"../topics/agent-containment/index.html\">Module 31, Agent code execution and containment</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>LLM07:2026 Misinformation</td><td>No lesson covers this entry. It is about model output that is incorrect or misleading and is trusted anyway. This course teaches the controls around a model (what its output may do, who approves it, what it can reach), not how to make its answers correct.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>LLM08:2026 Hidden Context Exposure</td><td><a href=\"../topics/data-in-model-context/index.html\">Module 24, Data in model context</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>LLM09:2026 Vector and Embedding Weaknesses</td><td><a href=\"../topics/supply-chain-retrieval-and-memory/index.html\">Module 25, Supply chain, retrieval, and memory</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>LLM10:2026 Improper Output Handling</td><td><a href=\"../topics/prompt-injection-and-output-handling/index.html\">Module 22, Prompt injection and output handling</a></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"agentic\">\n<h2 id=\"agentic\">OWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications for 2026</h2>\n<p class=\"meta\"><a href=\"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-top-10-for-agentic-applications-for-2026/\">OWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications for 2026</a>. Version 2026, released 9 December 2025.</p>\n<div class=\"wrap\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Entry</th><th>Lessons that cite it</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack</td><td><a href=\"../topics/prompt-injection-and-output-handling/index.html\">Module 22, Prompt injection and output handling</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation</td><td><a href=\"../topics/prompt-injection-and-output-handling/index.html\">Module 22, Prompt injection and output handling</a>; <a href=\"../topics/agent-authority-and-approvals/index.html\">Module 23, Agent authority and approvals</a>; <a href=\"../topics/logging-and-detection/index.html\">Module 30, Logging, detection and response</a>; <a href=\"../topics/agent-containment/index.html\">Module 31, Agent code execution and containment</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse</td><td><a href=\"../topics/credential-lifecycle/index.html\">Module 8, Workload and agent identity lifecycle</a>; <a href=\"../topics/delegation-and-token-exchange/index.html\">Module 19, Delegation and token exchange</a>; <a href=\"../topics/agent-containment/index.html\">Module 31, Agent code execution and containment</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>ASI04 Agentic Supply Chain Vulnerabilities</td><td><a href=\"../topics/supply-chain-retrieval-and-memory/index.html\">Module 25, Supply chain, retrieval, and memory</a>; <a href=\"../topics/model-supply-chain/index.html\">Module 32, Model and artifact supply chain</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>ASI05 Unexpected Code Execution (RCE)</td><td><a href=\"../topics/agent-containment/index.html\">Module 31, Agent code execution and containment</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>ASI06 Memory &amp; Context Poisoning</td><td><a href=\"../topics/supply-chain-retrieval-and-memory/index.html\">Module 25, Supply chain, retrieval, and memory</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>ASI07 Insecure Inter-Agent Communication</td><td><a href=\"../topics/agent-to-agent/index.html\">Module 21, Agent-to-agent (A2A)</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>ASI08 Cascading Failures</td><td><a href=\"../topics/agent-containment/index.html\">Module 31, Agent code execution and containment</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>ASI09 Human-Agent Trust Exploitation</td><td><a href=\"../topics/agent-authority-and-approvals/index.html\">Module 23, Agent authority and approvals</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>ASI10 Rogue Agents</td><td><a href=\"../topics/agent-containment/index.html\">Module 31, Agent code execution and containment</a></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"not-covered\">\n<h2 id=\"not-covered\">What the course does not cover</h2>\n<ul class=\"prose\">\n<li>The entries marked above as not covered or partly covered.</li>\n<li>Anything specific to GraphQL, gRPC or WebSocket. No lesson mentions them. The lessons use HTTP APIs that exchange JSON.</li>\n<li>How to test an API's security from the outside. The lessons list the negative tests their own controls must pass. No lesson teaches a testing method or a tool.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n"
}
